# Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX), from your GA4
# property's Admin → Data Streams → your stream → "Measurement ID".
#
# Leave this unset for local dev/preview — Analytics.astro renders nothing
# at all (no banner, no script) until it's set. To go live with analytics,
# set the same variable name on your host (e.g. Netlify → Site settings →
# Environment variables) and redeploy. Copy this file to .env and fill in
# the value if you want to test it locally first — .env is gitignored, so
# it never gets committed.
PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# Brevo (newsletter signup — see netlify/functions/subscribe.ts and README
# → "Newsletter signup"). BREVO_API_KEY has full account access, so treat
# it like a password: only ever set it as a Netlify environment variable
# (Site settings → Environment variables) for the live site — pasting it
# here is only for testing locally with `netlify dev` (NOT `astro dev`,
# which doesn't run Netlify Functions at all). BREVO_LIST_ID is the numeric
# id of the list your automation watches, from Brevo → Contacts → Lists.
BREVO_API_KEY=
BREVO_LIST_ID=
